            "title": "Broadcom earnings, Fed nomination, ADP data: What to Watch",
            "description": "<p>Market Domination Overtime host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> takes a look at the top stories for investors to watch on Thursday, Sept. 4.</p>\n<p>Companies like Broadcom (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AVGO\">AVGO</a>), Docusign (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/DOCU\">DOCU</a>), and Lululemon Athletica (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/LULU\">LULU</a>) will report their latest quarterly earnings results.</p>\n<p>The Senate Banking Committee will be holding a confirmation hearing for <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/stephen-miran-to-pledge-upholding-fed-independence-at-nomination-hearing-thursday-100039700.html\">prospective Fed governor Stephen Miran </a>tomorrow.</p>\n<p>Be on the lookout for the latest private-sector employment out from ADP.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination-overtime/\">Market Domination Overtime</a>.</p>",
